   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "I've done it.",
   "texto": [
    "Past passive participles are usually formed with perfect transitive verbs and describe the result: **прочитанная книга**, **написанное письмо**. The complete forms match in gender, number and case with the Russian noun: **книга** is feminine although «book» is masculine in Spanish.",
    "**-нн-** and **-т-** are common: **прочитать → прочитанный**, **написать → написанный**, **открыть → открытый**. Not all verbs form the participle on a regular basis; learn the frequent forms in context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The short form",
   "texto": [
    "As predicted, the passive participle usually has a short form: **дверь закрыта**, **письмо написано**, **окно открыто**. Concord in gender and number, but the short form is not decelerated per case.",
    "Imperfect verbs can also form passive participles of the present, such as **читаемый** (which is being read); they appear above all in formal records. In B1 it is appropriate to recognize them even if they are less practiced."
   ]
